tests:
  unit:
    waived: "TSDoc text only - four docstrings in ui/src/components/{Notice,CopyButton,TonedText,Field}.tsx. No markup, props, behaviour or export changed, so there is nothing a unit test can assert that it was not already asserting: the 741-test suite passes unchanged, which is the evidence that this commit moved no behaviour. The docstrings themselves are not inert, though - scripts/design-registry.mjs parses them into the roster the design flow reads, so the check that matters is that the roster still emits 28 entries with the corrected text, which it does."
verified:
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs - 28 entries, unchanged in count, with the corrected @use/@avoid/@anatomy lines."
  - "cd ui && pnpm test - 741 passed, 44 files, identical to before."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src - clean, including the design/vocabulary rule."
  - "cargo xtask gate0 - green."
  - "grep -rn 'HeaderTable|components\\.tsx' over ui/src/components/ returns nothing - the three dangling destinations are gone, and the sweep is the check, not a spot fix."
  - "The Field claim was checked against the built screen rather than assumed: ui/src/App.tsx renders Field at two call sites (free text, status) and Select at two (host, method), so 'four fields' was false and 'two typed keys' is true."
note: "A standalone commit on the epic branch, outside any WU, from a verified epic-scope finding. Three of the four are the exact defect class DEC-30 exists to name - a registry docstring redirecting to something that does not exist - and this epic created them by deleting HeaderTable (W6) and components.tsx (W2) without sweeping the contracts that cited them. The fourth is a tenancy claim W4 falsified when it turned two of Field's four named filter fields into Selects. None of the four is reachable by any mechanical check the repo has: the roster parses the tags but never resolves the prose inside them, which is why they survived eleven WU reviews and surfaced only at the epic seam."
